{
  "description": "Session profiles (SDN-40): the laptops of alice run under the SessionProfile laptops, which her Group staff gives, and the laptop of bob under contractors, which bob names himself over the profile of staff; srv-1 runs under none. Each Node judges a packet by the profile of its peer and by its own, before the policy. A TCP SYN to a laptop under no-server is dropped by the Node that sends it, while a SYN from one passes; the privacy filter keeps the two laptops of alice apart, while each reaches srv-1 and the laptop of bob; no-routing drops a packet to the outside of the 1:1 NAT rule of lap-a at srv-1, and one from the LAN behind lap-a at lap-a itself. Explain names the profile of each end and the resource that gives it.",
